  "title": "osf work-tracker command group",
  "summary": "Adds an `osf work-tracker` CLI group with two subcommands: `ready` reads the single GitHub Project item whose status is Ready, and `report` writes a state (in-progress, in-review, failed, blocked+cause) plus a recap file back to one item. A new `[work_tracker]` table in `osf.toml` (owner, project_number, status_field, skip_status) configures the GitHub adapter; the general config loader now strips that table so it does not trip `deny_unknown_fields`. The command layer is thin: it parses arguments, builds a real `GitHubWorkTracker` over the `gh` CLI, and delegates to the existing `work_tracker::ready::pick` and `work_tracker::report::finish_run`.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
